{
  "schemaVersion": "plate-normalisation-test-vectors-v1",
  "normalisationId": "mavi-plate-normalisation-v1",
  "rules": [
    "1. The input is well-formed Unicode text (no lone surrogates); a two-line reading is its lines joined by LF, top line first.",
    "2. Unicode NFKC.",
    "3. ASCII upper-case only: a-z become A-Z; no other character changes case (culture-invariant).",
    "4. Remove exactly these separators: U+0009 TAB, U+000A LF, U+000D CR, U+0020 SPACE, U+002D '-', U+002E '.', U+002F '/', U+003A ':', U+00B7 MIDDLE DOT. Nothing else is removed.",
    "5. If nothing remains: rejected, reason 'empty'. If any remaining character is outside [A-Z0-9]: rejected, reason 'non-alphanumeric'. A rejected reading has no normalised text and is never searchable; its raw text is kept.",
    "6. No confusable substitution (O/0, I/1, B/8, S/5, Z/2), no insertion, no deletion beyond rule 4, no grammar repair, no length rule.",
    "7. formatClass (advisory; only for 'ok'): 'in-bh' if ^[0-9]{2}BH[0-9]{4}[A-Z]{1,2}$, else 'in-standard' if ^[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{1,2}[A-Z]{0,3}[0-9]{1,4}$, else 'other'. It never changes the text and is not a validity claim."
  ],
